From 33ce7216a42372f914c125a917b7133fdf7296e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11-long frame contract (R7-A/C/D) - rate ref on
 sent frames, cooldown at the passive frame, passive on the longActive-off
 exit

Round-7 (G7-VERIFICATION.md) ran the real car layer frame-by-frame into the real compiled panda TX hook and
found three frame-contract defects, all safe-direction (the panda refuses; nothing commands more brake than
intended), but together they meant FCA11 delivered ~one 0.04 g frame per episode on the road for every
personality. None were introduced by G7; the rate-reference bug is pre-existing in the shipped build
(7f2ce281) and in G7 alike.

- R7-A (blocker, pre-existing): the panda allows +HYUNDAI_FCA11_LONG_RATE_STEP (4 = 0.04 g) over the last
  ACCEPTED frame (hyundai.h:940-941), but the car layer advances _dec_last_sent on EVERY 100 Hz frame while
  sending only on the 50 Hz slot. The SENT ramp therefore stepped +8 per sent frame and the panda refused
  every actuating frame after the first. Fix: advance _dec_last_sent only inside the send branch, i.e. only
  on frames actually sent (== the panda's last-accepted frame). The sent ramp is now 0 -> 0.30 g in 8 sent
  frames (160 ms), matching the panda comment.

- R7-C (major, in G7): the panda starts its cooldown on the ACCEPTED PASSIVE frame (hyundai.h:970-973), which
  on an odd-frame release goes out one frame later than the release. G7 stamped _budget_end at the release
  frame, so the first re-brake at exactly +300 frames was refused (and with R7-A desynchronised the rate
  reference for the whole next episode). Fix: stamp _budget_end when the passive frame is EMITTED, and add a
  conservative margin (FCA11_COOLDOWN_MARGIN_FRAMES = 2) so the Python mirror is a strict subset of what the
  panda allows rather than an exact copy.

- R7-D (major, in G7): the longActive-off exit cleared the mirror and owed no passive frame, but the panda's
  act_active survives a disengage (only hyundai_init clears it), so the next episode was cut early. Fix: on
  the longActive-off exit, if an episode was open keep _release_pending (do not clear the mirror), and emit
  the passive frame on the first longActive frame back, before any new actuation.

Invariant (new test): every episode that OPENS ends with exactly one passive 0x38D on EVERY exit path where
the panda episode state persists (brake / gas / gear / camera-owns / staleness / longActive-off); the disabled
path sends none (the panda re-arms on hyundai_init).

Validation (round 8): the round-7 panda co-sim (real car layer -> real compiled panda, 100 Hz, no shim) over
its 9 scenarios goes from 1481 refused frames (G7) to 0 (G8). Whole-drive model on replay149_composed.json:
delivered-brake share relaxed/standard/aggressive = 0.820 / 0.785 / 0.854 of intended (== the round-6
passive-only ceiling; >= the round-6 baseline), 0 unintended refusals. Car-layer tests 44 passed (the two
cooldown-origin tests updated for the +2-frame margin, 4 regressions added); panda Fca11Long subset 293
passed. Python-only: no opendbc/safety .h/.c change, the panda TX hook and budget code are untouched.
